<!--
  ============================================================================
  sitemap.xml — videoeditor.agency
  Owner: T9. Written 2026-09-05, once the pages actually existed.
  ============================================================================

  WHY THIS FILE DID NOT EXIST UNTIL NOW
  A sitemap is an ASSERTION that a list of URLs exists. On 2026-09-05 T9
  declined to write one because zero of the ten pages had been built and every
  line would have been false. T4, T6, T7 and T8 have since shipped. Every URL
  below was verified against the file it resolves to, in this folder, today.

  ⚠️ /portfolio/ IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. site/portfolio/ DOES NOT EXIST — T5
  has not run and is blocked on R07 (real portfolio items, still OPEN).
  Listing it would be the exact failure this file was postponed to avoid.
  ⚠️ AND IT IS NOT ONLY A SITEMAP PROBLEM: 60 of the 61 rows in _redirects
  point at /portfolio/. A 301 to a URL that 404s is worse than no redirect.
  /portfolio/ IS A HARD PRECONDITION OF CUTOVER. → T5, then add it here.

  ⚠️ /404.html IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT and always will be. It is the one page
  whose noindex never comes off — an indexed error page competes in search
  with the pages it exists to apologise for.

  ⚠️ THIS FILE IS INERT UNTIL T10. Every page below still carries
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">, and robots.txt still says
  Disallow: /. A sitemap listing noindexed pages on a disallowed site does
  nothing at all. Both locks move at cutover, in the order robots.txt sets
  out: LIFT THE META TAGS FIRST, PAGE BY PAGE, THEN OPEN robots.txt.

  NO <priority> AND NO <changefreq>. Google has ignored both for years.
  They are noise that invites arguments about numbers nobody acts on.

  <lastmod> IS THE DATE THE PAGE'S CONTENT WAS LAST WRITTEN, not the date this
  file was generated. ⚠️ IT MUST BE UPDATED WHEN A PAGE CHANGES. An always-
  current lastmod on an unchanged page teaches a crawler to ignore the field.
  Every page here was written on 2026-09-05, so today they are all the same —
  that will stop being true with the first edit after launch.
  ============================================================================
-->
